Venetium 0027 - chrome.dll links against the SDK 19041 ARM32 import libs: two newer GUIDs and IsWindowArranged.

BATCH-ARM-1 section 5, his decision (2026-10-04, "0027, also fix x86"). After 0026 the ARM32 chrome.dll link failed on 3 symbols the
Windows SDK 19041 ARM32 import libs do not have (D9: 26100 headers + 19041 ARM32 libs). 3 files:
- media/capture/video/win/video_capture_device_mf_win.cc: __uuidof(IMFCameraControlNotify) instead of IID_IMFCameraControlNotify
  (not in the 19041 ARM32 mfuuid.lib).
- ui/accessibility/platform/uia_client_info_source_win.cc: __uuidof(CUIAutomationClientInfoSource) instead of
  CLSID_CUIAutomationClientInfoSource (not in the 19041 ARM32 Uuid.Lib).
  Both uuids are the ones the 26100 headers declare (mfidl.h MIDL_INTERFACE("E8F2540D-..."), UIAutomationCore.h
  DECLSPEC_UUID("A8D4F123-...")) and are byte-identical to the symbols in the 26100 x86/x64 libs, so every arch gets the same GUID.
- chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_frame_view_win.cc: IsWindowArranged() is resolved at run time on every arch
  (IsWindowArrangedIfAvailable, via base::win::GetUser32FunctionPointer as win_util.cc does); where it is missing no window counts
  as arranged. The 19041 user32.lib (ARM32 and x86) has no stub for it, and user32.dll before Windows 10 does not export it -
  user32 is delay-loaded in chrome.dll, so on Windows 7/8.x the first GetWindowRoundedCorners() call would have hit the
  delay-load failure hook. (Windows 10 user32 exports it since RTM, chrome/test/delayload/supported_imports_10.0.10240.txt.)
Reviewed before capture by a read-only workflow (it corrected the first draft's comment, which claimed a static import).
Checked (RUNTIME, real arm-rt21 graph): the three ARM objects compile with no reference to the three symbols; chrome.dll and
venetium.exe then link as ARMNT. x86 (STRUCTURAL): browser_frame_view_win.cc compiled with out/x86-rt21's own command no longer
references __imp__IsWindowArranged@4.

